+/// Separator worker threads. This is part of the SEARCH, not just of how fast it runs: every worker
+/// owns an RNG seeded from the master and the best of their competing proposals is kept, so a different
+/// worker count explores a different sequence and lands on a different layout. It is therefore a
+/// constant — deriving it from the machine's core count (as this build used to, via
+/// `available_parallelism().clamp(3, 12)`) means the same job nests differently on different machines.
+pub const N_WORKERS: usize = 8;
